<title>USA: Ronson extends exchange offer.</title>
<headline>Ronson extends exchange offer.</headline>
<dateline>SOMERSET, N.J. 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ronson Corp said Monday that it has accepted 76 percent of its 12 percent cumulative convertible preferred stock in response to its offer to exchange 1.7 common shares for each preferred share, and the offer has been extended to May 16.</p>
<p>It had been scheduled to expire April 7.</p>
<p>The company said that aside from the extension, no other terms of the offer have been changed.</p>
<p>Ronson manufactures butane and liquid fuel lighters and other consumer products, as well as providing various services to the aviation industry.</p>
</text>
